WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.859 --> 00:00:05.819
In the entire history of the Soviet Union,
there was not a single planned and peaceful

00:00:05.819 --> 00:00:08.599
leadership transition.

00:00:08.599 --> 00:00:14.910
Of the eight Communist Party Secretaries in
the nearly seven decades between 1922 and

00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:22.210
91, six ruled until they died, one was overthrown,
and Gorbachev saw the dissolution of the entire

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:23.460
state.

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:29.810
In fact, there had never been a peaceful handover
of power in any major Communist country…

00:00:29.810 --> 00:00:37.130
until the early 2000s, when Chinese leader
Jiang Zemin voluntarily resigned.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:42.899
For the first time in the nation’s history,
there was no coup, no intrigue, no political

00:00:42.899 --> 00:00:44.719
infighting.

00:00:44.719 --> 00:00:51.260
Jiang Zemin even endorsed his successor, despite
having not chosen him.

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:56.180
No one was calling China a liberal democracy,
but it seemed as though the days of one-man

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:59.500
rule were finally over.

00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:01.910
Term limits were instituted.

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.300
Anyone over the age of 68 was expected to
retire.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:11.650
And each successive leader — from Mao Zedong
to Deng Xiaoping to Jiang Zemin to Hu Jintao

00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:15.270
— was less powerful than the last.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:20.340
The phrase being floated around at the time
was “intra-party democracy”.

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:25.060
In other words, there may only be one party,
but within it, there was plenty of room for

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:27.980
healthy competition.

00:01:27.980 --> 00:01:33.140
From here on out, policies would be debated,
leaders would rotate out, and the “best

00:01:33.140 --> 00:01:35.560
ideas” would win.

00:01:35.560 --> 00:01:42.579
…Then, one man — Xi Jinping — reversed
all this progress.

00:01:42.579 --> 00:01:45.950
Xi is about to begin his third term in office.

00:01:45.950 --> 00:01:52.130
And with neither a designated successor nor
hardly any competition, there’s no end to

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:54.320
his rule in sight.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:02.549
So, how did China revert from “intra-party
democracy” to one-man rule in a single generation?

00:02:02.549 --> 00:02:10.030
How does any of this — the Chinese Communist
Party — actually work?

